// ============================================================================
// CREATIVE HUB — the Studio board (v1 · round 1: the shell on real cards)
//
// Desktop-first board for the production stage: three tabs (Edit / Design /
// Approve), a table-first workspace with an optional card view, grouping,
// filters, search, bulk selection and the per-row "…" menu. Built from
// design-handoff-creative-hub/DESKTOP-SPEC.md; the prototype in that folder
// is the reference for anything the spec leaves open.
//
// Round 1 is READ-ONLY. Every card on the board is a real Content record
// already in the Studio (Status "Post Production" or "Ready to Post"). The
// buttons and menu rows are in place so the layout can be reviewed, but the
// ones that would change a record say so with a dark toast until the round
// that wires them. Nothing here writes to Airtable.
//
// Data (all read straight from the Softr datasources, no webhooks):
//   • Content — the cards. Which tab a card sits on comes from its Format
//     (video → Edit, graphic → Design) and its Post-production status.
//   • Brands — the Brand filter chips.
//   • Filming Sessions — the shoot-batch names, times and order.
// Round 2 adds Script Files, Uploads and Comments for the open-record view.
//
// Handoff: design-handoff-creative-hub/ (v3, 2026-09-14). v3 corrected the
// first spec, which was partly written from the mobile design. Board rules
// from v3 §16: a finished card lives on Approve and only returns to its queue
// tab when grouping by Status; settled Approve cards (Approved / Discarded)
// only show when grouping by Status; every tab count is the rows that tab
// renders under the current grouping, so counts move with Group by; Flowy
// never holds a To do. Where v3's prose and the preview disagree, the preview
// wins (approve cards DO show the due date while To approve).
//
// Status mapping (tolerant of the old queue names while they are renamed):
//   To do        ← New Shots · Creatives Queue · Flowy's Queue · To Design · To do · (empty)
//   In progress  ← In Progress
//   To approve   ← To Approve   (shows as "Edited" / "Designed" on the queue tabs)
//   Approved     ← Status "Ready to Post" (or Post-production status Approved)
//   Discarded    ← Discard · Discarded
// Who: a person = the Assignee link; Flowy = a record In progress with nobody
// assigned; otherwise Unassigned. Flowy never holds a To do (v3 §16.3), so a
// card still sitting in the old "Flowy's Queue" reads To do + Unassigned.
//
// Lifted verbatim from scripting-studio-v1.tsx: VIDEO/GRAPHIC format lists,
// graphic detection, stripRichText, formatDuration, toNum, formatRelativeDate,
// the paging helper, the toast helpers and the Flowy wave. Shoot-batch labels
// follow the design ("Tue Aug 11", "· 10:30"), not the studio's. Inline styles
// for every colour (Tailwind arbitrary colours do not render in Vibecode); the
// <style> tag only carries hover rules + keyframes.
//
// Board chrome matches the Scripting Studio, not the handoff, wherever the two
// disagreed (Karen, 2026-09-14): the "Creative Studio" title set like
// "Scripting Board", the studio's page grey, its segmented tabs and counts,
// its toolbar button inks, a Create button styled like "+ Script", and group
// headers that sit on the page above each group's own table, never inside one.
// The icon buttons stay 34px (a touch under the studio's) by Karen's choice.
// Round two: filters before search; hooks as plain 400 text; four-across
// cards (320px minimum); level footers; columns resized by dragging the
// heading dividers; a past due date shows as the date in red; and the table's
// three record states. A queue record (To do, In progress) expands to its lead
// field for the format plus creative direction, with Flowy · Assign · ⋯, and
// its collapsed row shows a chevron, not the ⋯. A record in the approval stage
// (To approve, Approved, Discarded, on any tab) never expands: a click opens
// the record window, and its row keeps the ⋯.
// Round three: the comment bubble and the arrow share each row's last cell,
// pinned to the visible edge; queue cards expand the studio's way (arrow after
// the bubble, first tap expands, second opens); status tags weigh 500 (cards
// 1px smaller); and the record window follows the studio's ScriptModal:
// header, 17.5/600 title, Card details (closed on open) with the script
// details plus assignee, due date and shoot batch, the grey tag rail, studio
// section labels, the small Add files button and the 36px footer.
// Round four (Karen, 2026-09-15): the window sits on the studio's layers
// (9998/9999) so Softr's sidebar can't cover its top-left buttons; up/down
// always show; the title folds into a thin header line on scroll; Card
// details = topic category, topic, duration (slides), content type, angle,
// inspo link, script or text overlay, shooting instructions (lighter boxes,
// thinner text); the rail = status, format, assignee, due date, shoot
// date (thinner text); the sections = on-screen hook or slides copy (closed,
// with an arrow), visual CTA (videos only), creative direction, captions &
// hashtags, with the files under the preview. The long fields come from a
// one-record read keyed on the table's "Self ID" (RECORD_ID()).
//
// Round five (Karen, 2026-09-15): the record window writes. The five tags,
// every Card details row except topic and its category, and every section's
// words change from here; an unsaved-changes bar takes the footer's place
// until you Save or Cancel, exactly as the Scripting Studio does.
// ============================================================================

